## Material design values
'<small>Source: NEN-EN 1992-1-1 tab. 2.1N; 3.1.6 (3.15), (3.16); 3.1.7 (3.17), (3.18); tab. 3.1; 3.2.7</small>
'<i>From strength class to design value, with the stress-strain diagram used for concrete in compression.</i>
f_ck = 30 N/mm^2', concrete C30/37<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
f_yk = 500 N/mm^2', reinforcing steel B500<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
γ_C = 1.5', table 2.1N<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
γ_S = 1.15', table 2.1N<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
α_cc = 1.0'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
ε_c2 = 0.002', table 3.1<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
ε_cu2 = 0.0035', table 3.1<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
f_cd = α_cc*f_ck/γ_C', (3.15)'
f_yd = f_yk/γ_S
f_ctm = 0.30*(f_ck/MPa)^(2/3)*MPa to N/mm^2', table 3.1'
f_ctd = 0.7*f_ctm/γ_C', (3.16)'
σ_c(ε) = f_cd*if(ε < ε_c2; 1 - (1 - ε/ε_c2)^2; 1)
#hide
PlotHeight = 220
#show
$Plot{σ_c(x/1000) @ x = 0 : 1000*ε_cu2}
'<span style="color:#D97706; font-weight:700;">━━ σ<sub>c</sub></span> &nbsp; parabola up to ε<sub>c2</sub>, constant beyond it, (3.17), (3.18). Horizontal axis: strain in ‰.
